{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>About this time tomorrow.</b> At this time tomorrow; He drew a line for him on the wall — tomorrow, when the sun reaches here, the hail will fall." "<b>Was founded.</b> That it was founded; and every word whose root begins with yod — such as יסד, ילד, ידע, יסר — when it is in the nif'al/bithpa'el, the vav comes in place of the yod, as in הִוָּסְדָהּ, הִוָּלְדָהּ (Hosea 2), וַיִּוָּדַע, ״וַיִּוָּלֵד לְיוֹסֵף״ (Genesis 46), ״בִּדְבָרִים לֹא יִוָּסֶר עֶבֶד״ (Proverbs 29)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:14.414303205Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}